---
import ExampleSource from '../../components/ExampleSource.astro';
import Sample from '../../examples/studio/app';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { samplesSource } from '../../lib/links';
import { sitePath } from '../../lib/site-path';
import modelSource from '@opsydyn/effect-three-samples/src/studio/model.ts?raw';
import messageSource from '@opsydyn/effect-three-samples/src/studio/message.ts?raw';
import updateSource from '@opsydyn/effect-three-samples/src/studio/update.ts?raw';
import sceneSource from '@opsydyn/effect-three-samples/src/studio/scene.ts?raw';
import viewSource from '@opsydyn/effect-three-samples/src/studio/view.ts?raw';
const sources = [{ name: 'model.ts', content: modelSource }, { name: 'message.ts', content: messageSource }, { name: 'update.ts', content: updateSource }, { name: 'scene.ts', content: sceneSource }, { name: 'view.ts', content: viewSource }];
---
<Layout title="Studio — effect-three">
  <section class="page-intro"><a class="text-link" href={sitePath('/examples/')}>← All examples</a><p class="eyebrow">LIGHT, MATERIAL, MOTION</p><h1>Drag it into the light.</h1><p>Five geometries in five material kinds under a sky light, a warm point light and a spot that follows your selection. Drag a piece across the floor, right-click to change its finish, double-click to send it home. Toggle shadows and filmic tone mapping, and switch between perspective, orthographic and a split view with a plan from above. The monitor at the back is a render texture: its own little scene showing your selection close up.</p></section>
  <Sample client:load noMeta />
  <noscript><p>This example needs JavaScript and WebGL to render the scene.</p></noscript>
  <section class="closing-callout"><h2>Drags as data.</h2><p>A press on a piece captures the pointer, so every move arrives as a typed Message carrying a world-space ray, even off the canvas. The update meets that ray with the floor plane and moves the piece; the scene eases it there. There are no refs and no per-frame callbacks: the Model holds where everything is.</p><a class="text-link" href={samplesSource + '/studio'}>Explore the example source →</a></section>
  <ExampleSource files={sources} />
</Layout>
